{"name":"Amourette","hex":"#c8c5d7","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"amourette","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A petty love affair.","The love grass, or quaking grass."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amourette"}],"entries":[{"title":"Senegalia riparia","blocks":[{"text":"Senegalia riparia, commonly known as catch & keep, calumbi, jurema-branca, acacia zarza, amourette, and fleur du ben-aimé, is a thorny flowering plant of the family Fabaceae. It is native to Hispaniola, Puerto Rico, the Virgin Islands, the Lesser Antilles,Trinidad, and northern South America."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Senegalia_riparia_syn._Piptadenia_retusa.jpg/330px-Senegalia_riparia_syn._Piptadenia_retusa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Senegalia_riparia","wikidata":"Q15535648"}],"images":[],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Grey heron (00129p)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg/500px-Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg","ratio":0.8691693290734824,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_heron_(00129p).jpg","share":0.553125},{"title":"Brosimum guianense (Aubl.) Huber - Flickr - Alex Popovkin, Bahia, Brazil (21)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Brosimum_guianense_%28Aubl.%29_Huber_-_Flickr_-_Alex_Popovkin%2C_Bahia%2C_Brazil_%2821%29.jpg/500px-Brosimum_guianense_%28Aubl.%29_Huber_-_Flickr_-_Alex_Popovkin%2C_Bahia%2C_Brazil_%2821%29.jpg","ratio":1.78173719376392,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brosimum_guianense_(Aubl.)_Huber_-_Flickr_-_Alex_Popovkin,_Bahia,_Brazil_(21).jpg","share":0.28375},{"title":"Brosimum guianense (Aubl.) Huber - Flickr - Alex Popovkin, Bahia, Brazil (10)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Brosimum_guianense_%28Aubl.%29_Huber_-_Flickr_-_Alex_Popovkin%2C_Bahia